<title>HONG KONG: HSBC hits all time high on warrant talks.</title>
<headline>HSBC hits all time high on warrant talks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC Holdings Plc hits all time high at HK$169.50, up HK$1.50 at midday on Monday on market talk that a major brokerage house is mulling a cover warrant issue on the stock, brokers said.</p>
<p>The brokerage planned to issue 75 million of HSBC Holdings warrants at a premium of 14.35 percent and gearing of 7.5 times, market sources said. Trading volume was moderate with 1.3 million shares worth HK$221 million changing hands. -- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6369</p>
